{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Hecke.SelfConjugateRowCap","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Hecke.SelfConjugateRowCap","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.SelfConjugateRowCap.no_selfConj_two_row_of_five_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.SelfConjugateRowCap.no_selfConj_two_row_of_five_le","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/SelfConjugateRowCap.lean#L106-L123","doc":"**No self-conjugate two-row shape has five or more cells.** The\ncontrapositive of `selfConj_two_row_size_le_four`, and the form the consequence\nis actually used in: a self-conjugate partition of `n ≥ 5` necessarily has\n`ℓ(λ) > 2`, hence `y_λ = 0` under convention D.\n\nThe rest of the chain lives in the content sibling\n`folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-coefficient-shadow-price.lean`,\nwhich the library tree cannot import (siblings sit outside the package globs):\n`shadow_price_eq_zero_of_weight_eq_zero` proves `w̃_λ = 0 → u*_λ = 0` from the\nclass field `C_eq : C λ = w̃_λ · h·⅟2`. Joined, they say **the Wigner mechanism\ncontributes nothing above `k = 4`** — only `λ = (2,2)` is left.\n\nBean `qou-w06d`; answers the successor `qou-a5jk` opened. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.SelfConjugateRowCap.not_selfConj_three_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.SelfConjugateRowCap.not_selfConj_three_one","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/SelfConjugateRowCap.lean#L102-L104","doc":"`(3,1)` is NOT — its conjugate `[2,1,1]` has three parts, which is the row\ncap biting. Included as the smallest concrete failure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.SelfConjugateRowCap.selfConj_two_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.SelfConjugateRowCap.selfConj_two_two","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/SelfConjugateRowCap.lean#L98-L100","doc":"`(2,2)` is self-conjugate: the `k = 4` survivor, and the one Wigner shadow\nprice the row cap leaves standing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.SelfConjugateRowCap.selfConj_two_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.SelfConjugateRowCap.selfConj_two_one","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/SelfConjugateRowCap.lean#L95-L96","doc":"`(2,1)` is self-conjugate: the `k = 3` survivor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.SelfConjugateRowCap.selfConj_two_row_size_le_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.SelfConjugateRowCap.selfConj_two_row_size_le_four","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/SelfConjugateRowCap.lean#L87-L93","doc":"**The size bound, and the consequence.** A self-conjugate shape with at most\ntwo rows has at most four cells — so under the row cap there is NO self-conjugate\npartition at any level `n ≥ 5`, and a mechanism resting on self-conjugate shadow\nprices has nothing to draw on above `k = 4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.SelfConjugateRowCap.selfConj_two_row_enum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.SelfConjugateRowCap.selfConj_two_row_enum","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/SelfConjugateRowCap.lean#L76-L85","doc":"**The enumeration.** With `1 ≤ b ≤ a`, the only self-conjugate two-row shapes\nare `(2,1)` and `(2,2)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.SelfConjugateRowCap.selfConj_forces_first_row_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.SelfConjugateRowCap.selfConj_forces_first_row_two","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/SelfConjugateRowCap.lean#L68-L74","doc":"**Self-conjugacy with two rows forces `a = 2`.** The conjugate has `a` parts\nand the original has `2`, so a shape equal to its own conjugate has `λ₁ = 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.SelfConjugateRowCap.conjTwoRow_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.SelfConjugateRowCap.conjTwoRow_length","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/SelfConjugateRowCap.lean#L62-L66","doc":"**The conjugate of a two-row shape has exactly `a` parts.** All the content\nis here: conjugating turns the FIRST ROW LENGTH into the ROW COUNT. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.SelfConjugateRowCap.conjTwoRow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.SelfConjugateRowCap.conjTwoRow","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/SelfConjugateRowCap.lean#L56-L60","doc":"Column heights of the two-row shape `(a, b)` with `b ≤ a`: `b` columns of\nheight `2`, then `a - b` columns of height `1`. This is the conjugate partition,\nwritten as a list of parts. ","signatureChunk":0}]}